flowchart TD
  AmbientAudio("<b>AmbientAudio</b><br/>Background sound: drone, ventilation, the danger layer that rises when you are seen, sudden silence on a warning")
  ArchiveDirector("<b>ArchiveDirector</b><br/>Chapter 5 The Archive (Thursday): a buzz gives you away -› SILENT MODE (the little bell, M); the noise meter (footsteps, Ctrl = quiet); the oldest book's stamp (SEARCH = 0467); search words you READ; the old books awaiting repair - turning the pages is louder than walking")
  AudioSynth("<b>AudioSynth</b><br/>Every sound in the game, generated in code (hum, drones, chimes, footsteps, voices, the climax chord)")
  DangerFX("<b>DangerFX</b><br/>Red vignette and colour fringing that grow while you are being seen")
  EndScreen("<b>EndScreen</b><br/>Page after each chapter: CAUGHT (retry), chapter complete (continue), or one of the two endings")
  Fluorescent("<b>Fluorescent</b><br/>Ceiling fluorescent light with buzz; neglected ones flicker")
  Footsteps("<b>Footsteps</b><br/>3D footsteps (and the warden's keys) so you can hear where a watcher is")
  GameFlow("<b>GameFlow</b><br/>Scene flow: Title -› Chapter 1-6 (Monday to Friday) -› End page (win: next chapter, caught: retry); saves progress and the player name")
  GameSpeed("<b>GameSpeed</b><br/>2x story speed (Tab, or the title page): dialogue, messages, typing, loading bars and scripted waits run twice as fast - walking and watchers don't")
  HumSource("<b>HumSource</b><br/>The girl who hums: 3D off-key anthem you find by listening (fades in only when close)")
  Interactable("<b>Interactable</b><br/>Anything the player can use with E (desk cubby, panel, phone, shoulder tap, seats, doors)")
  Level01Director("<b>Level01Director</b><br/>Chapter 1 The Lesson: walked to your seat, roll call, find the phone in the desk, codes from the lecture, tap the student with the chalk triangle")
  Level02Director("<b>Level02Director</b><br/>Chapter 2 Lunch: sweeping camera + Lunch Monitor, follow the humming, forward the message within reach, sneak to the STAFF door and down the stairs")
  Level03Director("<b>Level03Director</b><br/>Chapter 3 Lights Out: listen for the warden, hold Space to pretend to sleep, Contacts code from his room call, flash the screen at the window 3 times")
  Level04Director("<b>Level04Director</b><br/>Chapter 6 Inspection Day (Friday, the fifth day): get the phone back, the 1979 photo (Voss was Seat 31), desk inspection, final choice: hide it (THE SEAT) or send it to everyone (LIGHTS)")
  LevelDirectorBase("<b>LevelDirectorBase</b><br/>Shared chapter rules: one subtitle at a time, danger meter, 3 hidden warnings, objective panel, prompts, chapter cards")
  Loc("<b>Loc</b><br/>Language setting (English / 中文): inline pairs L(en, zh) for story text, and a table T(en) for data text (lecture lines, posters, photo captions)")
  LocTable("<b>LocTable</b><br/>Chinese text for everything that is stored as English data: scene posters, contacts, photos, lessons, labels")
  PatrolAI("<b>PatrolAI</b><br/>A walking watcher on a NavMesh (Lunch Monitor, night warden): roams, follows scripted routes, scans while waiting")
  PhoneController("<b>PhoneController</b><br/>The hidden phone: hold to raise, passcodes, app loading, Photos, Messages, Contacts, forward/reply tasks, notifications, danger shake")
  PhotoTarget("<b>PhotoTarget</b><br/>Something worth photographing with the phone's Camera app (Chapter 4 Picture Day)")
  PictureDayDirector("<b>PictureDayDirector</b><br/>Chapter 4 Picture Day (Wednesday): a gym full of students milling about; every so often a CLASS PHOTO countdown - get to your spot, phone down, hold still, smile. Between photos: CAMERA (1045), photograph 3 things without being reported")
  Pigeon("<b>Pigeon</b><br/>A courtyard pigeon outside the classroom windows: pecks, looks around, hops a little. Not monitored. ...Yet.")
  PlayerRig("<b>PlayerRig</b><br/>The player body: walk, pulled to the seat, seated look, inspect the desk cubby, lie down in bed")
  PosterEgg("<b>PosterEgg</b><br/>A poster that changes when you come close and look at it: a too-perfect smile, a glitch, an inedible lunch, a mirror (you, in uniform), a red X, or Voss")
  Readable("<b>Readable</b><br/>A poster / sign / label the player can read by walking up and looking at it: a thought, a Search keyword, or the poster answering back")
  TVStatic("<b>TVStatic</b><br/>A screen showing nothing but snow ('LIVE' with nobody on it) - flickering grey emission")
  TeacherAI("<b>TeacherAI</b><br/>The teacher on a NavMesh: lectures, writes on the board (back turned = safe), wanders, calls on you, comes to take the phone")
  TeacherVision("<b>TeacherVision</b><br/>Can a watcher see a point: range + view cone + line of sight (classmates, pillars and desks are cover)")
  TitleScreen("<b>TitleScreen</b><br/>Title page: New Game (asks your name) / Continue / Chapters / Quit")
  UIFactory("<b>UIFactory</b><br/>Builds every on-screen panel, text, button and world-space poster canvas in code (no prefabs), with the right font for English or Chinese")

